        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Buddhist’s priests robe (<i>kesa</i>) of traditional patched style. The silk has a satin weave ground, with polychrome patterning wefts forming the design of birds among scrolling peonies. Six additional patches at the four corners and centre top have a smaller scale design of flower and phoenix bands in colours on a white ground. The lining is of blue shot silk."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/89b07160-0e5f-3a9b-9c17-1346541e6917> .

